{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793046085,"nonce":"crzF0Hpv7chwebA99TxHp5tOtjQ=","message":"Implemented in 7374a19361bf243f86f0cdb37e78c5123dd23464.\n\nThe Rust native/runner now provides authenticated, owner/repository-bound provisioning through MSB 0.7.11 on the NUC. It uses bounded bare checkout/archive extraction with host hooks and filters disabled, private durable registry state, single-writer and per-workspace work leases, admission limits, label-verified cleanup and explicit deletion/credential rotation. Guest command transport uses the session's new framed stdin/stdout bridge. No guest ports are published, and the private gateway credential stays outside the guest.\n\nVerified on real NUC KVM guests: concurrent duplicate opens; owner isolation; invalid credentials and owner mismatches; quotas; rejected symlink checkout and successful retry; guest environment/process/Git-config credential containment; interleaved large UTF-8 replies; runner shutdown/restart retaining files, identity and credentials; lost-guest refusal; idempotent deletion and generation/credential rotation. All test guests were removed. An idle private runner remains available over loopback SSH forwarding for further local development.\n\nThe full WASM browser flow passed through the locally emulated Rust Cloudflare Worker into the real NUC runner and MSB guest: GitHub chooser/sign-in fixture, short workspace URL, editing, durable unsaved journals, Save, reload, and sign-out/connection cleanup. The restored-dirty-buffer browser regression also passed. Native session tests (54), runner unit tests (4), real MSB integration (1), Worker tests (18), and browser-session tests (39) passed. WASM and native session were rebuilt; the tested bundle was staged at bin/web/rayde and the existing local session restarted with URL/credentials/state preserved.\n\nThis completes the local provisioning milestone, not full automatic VM restoration or production deployment. Missing/changed compute returns recovery-required rather than silently recloning. AutomaticRestore remains false. Toolchain images, filesystem/Git manifests and external-write reconciliation, stable path identities, fenced replacement and restore orchestration remain under the parent tracks. Real Cloudflare account resources are not needed yet.","files":null}]}